# AI Assistant Rules, GlobeTrotter

Full source of truth: `docs/AI_RULES.md`. Read that file before generating or editing any code.

Also read: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`, `docs/GlobeTrotter_MVP_Plan.md`.

## 1. Do not hallucinate

- Verify libraries against `requirements.txt` / `package.json`.
- Verify model fields against `backend/app/models/`.
- Verify routes against `backend/app/routers/` (source of truth).
- Never invent env vars, APIs, or claim unobserved success.
- Re-read files before editing.

## 2. Stay within scope

- Model changes require a matching Alembic migration in the same change.
- Do not touch routers outside the assigned module (see ownership table).
- Prefer the smallest change; follow existing patterns.
- If ambiguous, ask.

## 3. Security

- No hardcoded secrets; use `backend/app/core/config.py`.
- Ownership checks on user data; `require_role("admin")` for `/admin/*`.
- Only `GET /public/:slug` may skip auth.
- SQLAlchemy only (no string-built SQL); Pydantic for request bodies.
- CORS only `FRONTEND_URL`, never `*` with credentials.
- Pin dependency versions.

## 4. When unsure

Say so. Honest uncertainty beats a confident wrong answer.
